{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting Lost", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Should We Ask for Help?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe places, neighborhoods and countries in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Modal Should for Suggestions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal verb should to offer suggestions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "He should see the exhibition in Boston. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The form is:<br /> subject + modal verb + main verb<br />We&nbsp &nbsp&nbsp&nbsp &nbsp  &nbsp &nbsp   should  &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp  visit &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp the art gallery! ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They should go to the harbor area for lunch. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should ask for directions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There is only one form of should. It does not change.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking and Saying Where Places Are", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Simple Present tense to ask and say where places are. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you ask where a place is, you say:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Where is _____ ? <br/>Is ______ near here?<br/> What street is _____ on?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To say where a place is, you use prepositions and directions. <br/> _____ <span class=\"italic\"> is on ______ Street. <br/>It's south on  ______ Street.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you do not know where a place is, you say:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'm sorry, I don't know.<br/>I'm sorry, I have no idea.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Cultural Tip <br/>Saying<span class=\"italic\"> \"I have no idea.\" </span>without<span class=\"italic\"> \"I'm sorry,\"</span> is not very polite.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Response</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Where is Exhibition Place?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It's by the harbor.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Is  Exhibition Place near here?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Yes. It's south on Liberty Street.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What street is  Exhibition Place on?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm sorry, I have no idea.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "city hall ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the building for a city government ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The new city hall is on the next street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le09ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about places in a city.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "art gallery ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building to show paintings and sculpture", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The art gallery is showing paintings by Picasso.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le09ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gas station", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place to buy gasoline and oil", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's stop at the gas station. We need gas!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le09ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "convenience store ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a store in a busy area, open late, with everyday items to buy ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's stop at the convenience store. I need to buy milk.", "type": "example"},